<div class="commentContainer">
  <div class="commentSubject">
  <div class="wiki wikiPage" id="content_view">
  <ul><li>Born 21 January 1844, son of <a class="wiki_link" href="/web/20140707112902/http://bartonhistory.wikispaces.com/Rev.+Spencer+Ruthven+Thornton+%281813-1850%29">Rev. Spencer Ruthven Thornton (1813-1850)</a> and <a class="wiki_link" href="/web/20140707112902/http://bartonhistory.wikispaces.com/Caroline+Adelaide+Dupre+%281815-1898%29">Caroline Adelaide Dupre (1815-1898)</a>.</li><li>Married firstly (on 10 July 1866 in Croydon, Surrey), <a class="wiki_link" href="/web/20140707112902/http://bartonhistory.wikispaces.com/Fanny+Barton+%281841-1878%29">Fanny Barton (1841-1878)</a>.</li><li>Married secondly (on 19 September 1882 in High Cross, Ware, Hertfordshire), <a class="wiki_link" href="/web/20140707112902/http://bartonhistory.wikispaces.com/Alice+Henrietta+Giles+Puller+%281852-1930%29">Alice Henrietta Giles Puller (1852-1930)</a>.</li><li>Died 25 April 1921, aged 77.</li></ul><br/>
&quot;<em>After the funeral we left Buxton, and spent the remainder of July at Matlock; Aunt Fannie was with us, and two of her children. August at Retford, in Nottinghamshire; and September at <span style="background-attachment: initial; background-clip: initial; background-color: initial; url(https://web.archive.org/web/20140707112902im_/http://bartonhistory.wikispaces.com/ /www.wikispaces.com/i/a.gif); background-origin: initial; background-position: 100% 50%; background-repeat: no-repeat no-repeat; cursor: pointer; padding-right: 10px;"><a class="wiki_link_ext" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20140707112902/http://maps.google.co.uk/maps?q=southwold&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;hq=&amp;hnear=Southwold,+Suffolk,+United+Kingdom&amp;gl=uk&amp;ei=7UPyTLqbEsHChAe91-XxCw&amp;oi=geocode_result&amp;ved=0CCIQ8gEwAA&amp;z=13" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Southwold</a></span>, where <strong>Uncle Claude Thornton</strong>, and your <a class="wiki_link" href="/web/20140707112902/http://bartonhistory.wikispaces.com/Fanny+Barton+%281841-1878%29">Aunt Fanny</a> his wife, then lived at the Vicarage. She was a very fine woman, both in looks and in character; and her five children were of the same ages as our, from Jack to Jessie. I think this was the last time we saw her - for her children alas! were left motherless less than 18 months later.</em>&quot; <span style="cursor: pointer;"><a class="wiki_link" href="/web/20140707112902/http://bartonhistory.wikispaces.com/%2AMemoirs+of+Emily+Elliott#81">*Memoirs of Emily Elliott p81</a></span><br/>
<br/>
<!-- ws:start:WikiTextHeadingRule:0:&lt;h1&gt; --><h1 id="toc0"><a name="Children"></a><!-- ws:end:WikiTextHeadingRule:0 -->Children</h1>
 <br/>
With <a class="wiki_link" href="/web/20140707112902/http://bartonhistory.wikispaces.com/Fanny+Barton+%281841-1878%29">Fanny Barton (1841-1878)</a>:<br/>
<ol><li>Claude Dupre Thornton (1867-1934)</li><li>Adelaide Frances Thornton (1869-1947)</li><li>Cecil Bernard Thornton (1870-1886)</li><li>Douglas Montague Thornton (1873-1907)</li><li>Evelyn Maude Thornton (1874-1944)</li><li>Elsie Thornton (d.1963)</li><li>Chrissie Thornton</li></ol><br/>
With <span style="cursor: pointer;"><a class="wiki_link" href="/web/20140707112902/http://bartonhistory.wikispaces.com/Alice+Henrietta+Giles+Puller+%281852-1930%29">Alice Henrietta Giles Puller (1852-1930)</a></span>:<br/>
<ol><li>Reginald Christopher Thornton (1883-1978)</li><li>Lionel Spencer Thornton (1885-1960)</li><li>Bernard Thornton (1886-1908)</li><li>Katherine Emily Cecilia Thornton (1888-1964)</li><li>Winnifred Mary Thornton (1889-1965)</li><li>Elsie Caroline Thornton (1890-1963)</li><li>Alice Nora Thornton (1892-1914)</li><li>Christabel Monica Thornton (1893-1970)</li></ol>
